{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2\n  ucas: range it\nrange of it -> u8:\n  0..249   (44 distinct values)\n  values: 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64..65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121, 129, 132, 137, 144..145, ...\n  fits in u8\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what is the range of x squared for x an unsigned byte", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: u8) = x^2", "range it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "range", "type": "u8", "empty": false, "exhaustive": true, "points": 256, "undefined_points": 0, "min": {"value": 0, "exact": "0"}, "max": {"value": 249, "exact": "249"}, "distinct": 44, "values": [0, 1, 4, 9, 16, 17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64, 65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121, 129, 132, 137, 144, 145, 153, 161, 164, 169, 177, 185, 193, 196, 201, 209, 217, 225, 228, 233, 241, 249], "fits": "u8"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "every point of the domain evaluated"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2\n  ucas: range it\nrange of it -> u8:\n  0..249   (44 distinct values)\n  values: 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64..65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121, 129, 132, 137, 144..145, ...\n  fits in u8\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1\n  ucas: wrap it\nwrap analysis of it:\n  2x   (i8)\n      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen\n  2x + 1   (i8)\n      nuw holds\n      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)\n  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      exact for: -64..63\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "does x times 2 plus 1 overflow for a signed byte x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1", "wrap it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "wrap", "exhaustive": true, "operations": [{"op": "2x", "type": "i8", "nuw": false, "unsigned_wrap_points": 128, "unsigned_wrap_example": "x=-128", "nsw": false, "signed_wrap_points": 128, "signed_wrap_example": "x=-128", "c_ub": true}, {"op": "2x + 1", "type": "i8", "nuw": true, "unsigned_wrap_points": 0, "nsw": true, "signed_wrap_points": 0, "c_ub": false}], "end_to_end": {"exact": false, "mismatch_points": 128, "mismatch_example": "x=-128", "exact_for": [[-64, 63]]}}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1\n  ucas: wrap it\nwrap analysis of it:\n  2x   (i8)\n      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen\n  2x + 1   (i8)\n      nuw holds\n      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)\n  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      exact for: -64..63\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x*x\n  ucas: that(x: u8) = x^2\n  ucas: equiv it that\nit and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x times x the same as x squared for an unsigned byte x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: u8) = x*x", "that(x: u8) = x^2", "equiv it that"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "equiv", "equal": true, "exhaustive": true, "mismatch_points": 0, "method": "exhaustive"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "every point of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x*x\n  ucas: that(x: u8) = x^2\n  ucas: equiv it that\nit and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^3 - 3*x\n  ucas: crit it\ncritical points of it:\n  it' = 3x^2 - 3\n  x ≈ -1: local maximum, it = 2\n  x ≈ 1: local minimum, it = -2\n  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what are the critical points of x cubed minus 3x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = x^3 - 3*x", "crit it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "crit", "derivative": "3x^2 - 3", "points": [{"x": -1, "kind": "local maximum", "value": 2}, {"x": 1, "kind": "local minimum", "value": -2}]}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "sign changes of the derivative on a grid, refined by bisection"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^3 - 3*x\n  ucas: crit it\ncritical points of it:\n  it' = 3x^2 - 3\n  x ≈ -1: local maximum, it = 2\n  x ≈ 1: local minimum, it = -2\n  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(x^2)\n  ucas: diff it x\nd/dx it = 2x*cos(x^2)\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-10)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the derivative of sin x squared with respect to x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = sin(x^2)", "diff it x"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "diff", "vars": ["x"], "order": 1, "derivative": "2x*cos(x^2)"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 201, "max_diff": 3.191712493123741e-10, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(x^2)\n  ucas: diff it x\nd/dx it = 2x*cos(x^2)\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-10)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^2*sin(x)\n  ucas: integrate it from 0 to pi\n∫ x^2*sin(x) dx\n  = 2x*sin(x) + 2cos(x) - x^2*cos(x) + C\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 8.9e-16)\n  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 5.86960440108936\n  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 5.86960440108936, estimated error 6.5e-14\n  the two agree to 0\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the integral of x squared times sin x from 0 to pi", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = x^2*sin(x)", "integrate it from 0 to pi"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "integrate", "var": "x", "integrand": "x^2*sin(x)", "antiderivative": "2x*sin(x) + 2cos(x) - x^2*cos(x)", "definite": {"from": 0, "to": 3.141592653589793, "symbolic": 5.869604401089359, "numeric": 5.869604401089359, "error_estimate": 6.456564841198295e-14, "evaluations": 15, "value": 5.869604401089359}}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "derivative", "points": 401, "max_diff": 8.881784197001252e-16, "passed": true, "text": "d/dx of the antiderivative against the integrand"}, {"kind": "numeric_integral", "points": 15, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "F(b) - F(a) against adaptive Gauss-Kronrod"}], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^2*sin(x)\n  ucas: integrate it from 0 to pi\n∫ x^2*sin(x) dx\n  = 2x*sin(x) + 2cos(x) - x^2*cos(x) + C\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 8.9e-16)\n  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 5.86960440108936\n  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 5.86960440108936, estimated error 6.5e-14\n  the two agree to 0\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  ucas: show it\nit(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  -> int\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the sum of i squared for i from 1 to n", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)", "show it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "show", "definition": "it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)", "body": "sum(i, 1, n, i^2)", "type": "int"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  ucas: show it\nit(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  -> int\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 8, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)\n  ucas: show it\nit(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)\n  -> int\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the product of i for i from 1 to n", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)", "show it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "show", "definition": "it(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)", "body": "prod(i, 1, n, i)", "type": "int"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)\n  ucas: show it\nit(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)\n  -> int\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  ucas: closed it\nsum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the closed form of the sum of i squared for i from 1 to n", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)", "closed it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "closed", "loops": [{"loop": "sum(i, 1, n, i^2)", "closed_form": "n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6", "accepted": true, "checked": true, "method": ["Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)"]}]}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "iteration", "points": 101, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "against direct iteration on every point of the domain"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "equals direct iteration on every point of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  ucas: closed it\nsum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2 + 1\n  ucas: find it 2\nfind it: 256 points, computing in u8, costs from gt1030\n  cost 3   x*x + 1                                  affine fit\n  cost 4   x^2 + 1                                  polynomial (Horner)\n  [searched every term up to cost 4: 65536 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "find 2 cheaper implementations of x squared plus 1 for an unsigned byte x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: u8) = x^2 + 1", "find it 2"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "find", "points": 256, "sampled": false, "type": "u8", "model": "gt1030", "peephole": [], "implementations": [{"cost": 3, "expr": "x*x + 1", "why": "affine fit", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}, {"cost": 4, "expr": "x^2 + 1", "why": "polynomial (Horner)", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}]}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2 + 1\n  ucas: find it 2\nfind it: 256 points, computing in u8, costs from gt1030\n  cost 3   x*x + 1                                  affine fit\n  cost 4   x^2 + 1                                  polynomial (Horner)\n  [searched every term up to cost 4: 65536 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}, "isError": false}}
